{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795255325,"nonce":"akduKAzi+U0vWrj3HocOCxp0/JU=","title":"Clear the watch owner once its grace period runs out","message":"Found in the repo audit, 2026-11-21.\n\nengine::watch::Gate keeps owner after GRACE_MS runs out; only admission() stops honouring the\nstale grace_until. So: watch A loses its link and leaves; the grace expires. Later A connects\nwithout subscribing (a sensor search, say) and its link is lost again. disconnected() still sees A\nas owner and starts a fresh grace, and every other watch is locked out for 2 min, with nothing in\nthe log saying why.\n\nFix: in Gate::connected, when admission is Anyone, reset (*self = Self::new()) before returning\ntrue. Safe because a connect only happens while no other central is on.\n\nTest in watch.rs: lost at 0, connect at GRACE_MS + 1 without subscribing, lost again, admission is\nstill Anyone.","files":null}]}